Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35)
Recommends: libx11-6, libxkbcommon0, libwayland-client0, fonts-noto-cjk
Homepage: https://github.com/SosomLab/nexa-dir3
Description: Cross-platform lightweight dual-panel file explorer
 Nexa Dir is a lightweight dual-panel file explorer that looks and behaves the
 same on Windows, macOS and Linux. It is a single executable written in Rust
 that draws its own UI (no Qt, WebView or Electron).
 .
 Features: tabs, inline tree, preview pane (text, images, archive listings,
 WASM plugins), built-in terminal, batch rename, checksums, duplicate finder,
 folder compare and sync, favorites, trash with restore. User data lives in
 ~/.config/nexa-dir. License: PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 (noncommercial use
 only).
